              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %em polynomial
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an element of a
            %strong polynomial ring
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            whose elements are called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"}> variables
            ” or “indeterminates”, and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to R[X]
            to (the underlying set of) a commutative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[X]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            commutative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[X]
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Much like “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"}> vector
              ”, the term “polynomial” in this sense may seem slightly deprecated from the viewpoint of modern mathematics. We no longer think of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              as consisting of things called “vectors” (i.e. we don’t assign an objective meaning to “vectors”); it’s the other way around, where we introduce a type of structure called a vector space and then, relative to a given vector space context, declare that “vector” just means an element therein. Similarly, the term “polynomial” in the sense above has seemingly been subordinated to the structural concept of a polynomial ring. (In Linderholm’s
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mathematics Made Difficult
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0 + a_1 X + a_2 X^2 + \ldots + a_n X^n
              and asks “Well, how about it? Is it a polynomial, or isn’t it?” and the respondent says, “Yeah, sure, I guess. Looks like one. Yeah, sure, that’s a polynomial all right” – an answer which is not wrong exactly, but not quite right either, since it fails to recognize that there is something questionable about the question.)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              On further reflection, we might more objectively identify the concept of a “polynomial” (let us say a polynomial in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              variables) with a definable
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} ary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} operation
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
              of commutative
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi CommAlg
                      %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: CommAlg_R \to Set
              is the forgetful functor, a definable
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n \to U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[n] = R[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n \to U
              is canonically identified with a transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(R[x_1, \ldots, x_n], -) \to U
              or to an element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U R[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              stands for the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^{th}
              projection map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^n \to U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 x_2 \in R[x_1, x_2, x_3]
              is that it is the definable operation whose instantiation at any commutative
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^3 \to A
              taking
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b, c)
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b
            %p Of course, there are traditional standard expressions that people usually have in mind when they speak of a “polynomial” as such. But leaving it at that, where polynomials are merely identified with certain types of expressions (as by the characters in Linderholm’s book), ignores the deeper objective meaning of definable operations which of course is the actual point of it all.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Finally, sometimes “polynomial” is construed to mean a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+function"} polynomial function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[x]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ev
                          %mi R
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U R[x] \cong \hom(U, U) \stackrel{ev_R}{\to} \hom(U R, U R)
            %p
              where the second map sends a natural transformation to its component at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              as an
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(U R, U R)
              carries a commutative
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[x] \to \hom(U R, U R)
              that sends ‘
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              ’ to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+map"} identity map
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/value"} value
              of a polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in R[x]
              under this map is then the corresponding polynomial function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U R \to U R
            %p
              This conflation of polynomials with polynomial functions is often forgivable, particularly in those cases where the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[x] \to \hom(U R, U R)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
              (so that ‘polynomials’ are identified with certain types of functions). Of course the map
              %em won’t
              be injective if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(x)
              for a polynomial
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p With these preliminary remarks out of the way, we recall some of the more syntactic considerations with an example.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The set of
              %strong polynomials
              in one
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %strong univariate polynomials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[\mathbb{N}]
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
              on elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z^n
              of the variable
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mi z
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_n z^n + \cdots + a_1 z + a_0
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is an arbitrary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0, \dots, a_n \in R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} modulo
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
              generated by equations of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mi z
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mi z
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 z^{n+1} + a_n z^n + \cdots + a_1 z + a_0 = a_n z^n + \cdots + a_1 z + a_0
            %p
              so that we ignore coefficients of zero). (The
              %strong degree
              of a polynomial is the maximum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n
              is nonzero, in which case the
              %strong leading term
              of the polynomial is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n z^n
              %strong constant
              if its degree is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
              or as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              is possible if one is prepared to observe some fine print.
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em Chacun à son goût
            %p
              This set is equipped with an
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[z]
              and called the
              %strong polynomial ring
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %strong ring of polynomials
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R[z] \cdot R[z] \to R[z]
            %p the unique one that bilinearly extends the multiplication of monomials given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi l
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi l
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    z^k \cdot z^l = z^{k+l}
                    \\,.
          %p
            Thus, one way to construct a polynomial ring is to first construct the free commutative monoid generated by a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (the monoid of monomials), and then to construct the free
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            In addition to the ring structure, there is a further operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[z] \times R[z] \to R[z]
            which may be described as “substitution” or “composition”; see Remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#substitution"}
            below for a general description (which applies in fact to any
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              In the case of univariate polynomials, since the function type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[z] \to R[z]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebra"}
                function
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"}
                commutative
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              to constant functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C:R \to (R[z] \to R[z])
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[z]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:R[z] \to (R[z] \to R[z])
              inductively defined by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(s(r)) \coloneqq C(r)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(z) \coloneqq id_{R[z]}
              %strong substitution
              or
              %strong composition
              of univariate polynomials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \circ (-):R[z] \times R[z] \to R[z]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uncurrying"} uncurrying
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \circ q \coloneqq i(p)(q)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
